{"id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:gradient-characterization","title":"lem:gradient-characterization","path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.md","line":1032,"body":"","kind":"lemma","status":"not_started","tex":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex#lem:gradient-characterization","uses":["[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:gradient]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:sharp-map]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:flat-bijective]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","label":"lem:gradient-characterization","line":1601,"source":"\\begin{lemma}[Characterization of the gradient]\n\\label{lem:gradient-characterization}\n\n\\uses{def:gradient, def:sharp-map}\n\n\n\n\nLet $(M,g)$ be a finite-dimensional Riemannian manifold and $f\\colon M\\to\\mathbb R$\nsmooth. For every $p\\in M$ and $w\\in T_pM$,\n\\[\ndf_p(w)=\\langle\\operatorname{grad}f|_p,w\\rangle.\n\\]\nMoreover, $\\operatorname{grad}f|_p$ is the unique vector with this property.\n\\end{lemma}\n\n\\begin{proof}\n\n\\uses{def:gradient,def:sharp-map,lem:flat-bijective}\n\\sketch Apply the defining identity for $\\sharp$ to $\\alpha=df_p$. If $v$ satisfies the\nsame identity, then $v^\\flat=(\\operatorname{grad}f|_p)^\\flat$, so injectivity of\n$\\flat$ gives $v=\\operatorname{grad}f|_p$.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Lemma</div></section>[Characterization of the gradient] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6c656d3a6772616469656e742d636861726163746572697a6174696f6e\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Agradient\">↗ def:gradient</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Asharp-map\">↗ def:sharp-map</a> <p></p>Let <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(M,g)$\">$(M,g)$</span> be a finite-dimensional Riemannian manifold and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$f\\colon M\\to \\mathbb R$\">$f\\colon M\\to \\mathbb R$</span> smooth. For every <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$p\\in M$\">$p\\in M$</span> and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$w\\in T_pM$\">$w\\in T_pM$</span>, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[  df_p(w)=\\langle \\operatorname {grad}f|_p,w\\rangle .  \\]\">\\[  df_p(w)=\\langle \\operatorname {grad}f|_p,w\\rangle .  \\]</span> Moreover, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\operatorname {grad}f|_p$\">$\\operatorname {grad}f|_p$</span> is the unique vector with this property.  <p></p><section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Agradient\">↗ def:gradient</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Asharp-map\">↗ def:sharp-map</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Aflat-bijective\">↗ lem:flat-bijective</a> \\sketch Apply the defining identity for <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\sharp $\">$\\sharp $</span> to <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\alpha =df_p$\">$\\alpha =df_p$</span>. If <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$v$\">$v$</span> satisfies the same identity, then <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$v^\\flat =(\\operatorname {grad}f|_p)^\\flat $\">$v^\\flat =(\\operatorname {grad}f|_p)^\\flat $</span>, so injectivity of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\flat $\">$\\flat $</span> gives <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$v=\\operatorname {grad}f|_p$\">$v=\\operatorname {grad}f|_p$</span>. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:gradient","next":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:gradient-orthogonal-kernel","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:gradient","title":"def:gradient","label":"def:gradient"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:sharp-map","title":"def:sharp-map","label":"def:sharp-map"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:flat-bijective","title":"lem:flat-bijective","label":"lem:flat-bijective"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:gradient-orthogonal-kernel","title":"lem:gradient-orthogonal-kernel","label":"lem:gradient-orthogonal-kernel"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:gradient-eq-zero-iff","title":"lem:gradient-eq-zero-iff","label":"lem:gradient-eq-zero-iff"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:gradient-orthogonal-iff","title":"lem:gradient-orthogonal-iff","label":"lem:gradient-orthogonal-iff"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:gradient-characterization","title":"prop:gradient-characterization","label":"prop:gradient-characterization"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:transversal-representative-eq-gradient","title":"lem:transversal-representative-eq-gradient","label":"lem:transversal-representative-eq-gradient"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prob:gradient-characterization","title":"prob:gradient-characterization","label":"prob:gradient-characterization"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:gradient-characterization","title":"lem:gradient-characterization","tex":"\\begin{lemma}[Characterization of the gradient]\n\\label{lem:gradient-characterization}\n\n\\uses{def:gradient, def:sharp-map}\n\n\n\n\nLet $(M,g)$ be a finite-dimensional Riemannian manifold and $f\\colon M\\to\\mathbb R$\nsmooth. For every $p\\in M$ and $w\\in T_pM$,\n\\[\ndf_p(w)=\\langle\\operatorname{grad}f|_p,w\\rangle.\n\\]\nMoreover, $\\operatorname{grad}f|_p$ is the unique vector with this property.\n\\end{lemma}\n\n\\begin{proof}\n\n\\uses{def:gradient,def:sharp-map,lem:flat-bijective}\n\\sketch Apply the defining identity for $\\sharp$ to $\\alpha=df_p$. If $v$ satisfies the\nsame identity, then $v^\\flat=(\\operatorname{grad}f|_p)^\\flat$, so injectivity of\n$\\flat$ gives $v=\\operatorname{grad}f|_p$.\n\\end{proof}","source":"tex/references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:gradient","title":"def:gradient","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:sharp-map","title":"def:sharp-map","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:flat-bijective","title":"lem:flat-bijective","description":""}],"dependencies_omitted":0,"unresolved_dependencies":[],"unresolved_omitted":0}}